{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>My strength and my song, etc.</b> Now, the order for those who stand before HaShem to sing and to praise and to pray is to begin with matters grasped from HaShem toward oneself, and afterward with that grasped from HaShem toward one's forefathers — as we find that the Men of the Great Assembly established in the blessing of the Patriarchs: first ״אֱלֹהֵינוּ״ and afterward ״אֱלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵינוּ״. And therefore they arranged at the beginning of the song that which had reached them from His goodness, and said: ״עָזִּי וְזִמְרָת יָהּ וַיְהִי לִי לִישׁוּעָה״ — and this is what HaShem graced them with, to save them from the trouble they were in before the appointed end would arrive, and this was by virtue of His mercy toward them, as I have written on this matter at length in parashat Shemot (Exodus 3:7), and in parashat Va'era (Exodus 6:3). And therefore they concluded by saying <b>זֶה אֵלִי</b> and afterward said <b>אֱלֹהֵי אָבִי</b> — corresponding to the very order that the Men of the Great Assembly established to say ״אֱלֹהֵינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵינוּ״; and here they used singular language because all of them became as one person, as I explained in connection with the verse ״וַיֹּאמְרוּ לֵאמֹר״."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:18.827392959Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}